  "description": "Shapestatic is a climbing structure made of big geometric shapes. A blue sphere and a red cube cage are joined by rope nets, and children crawl through and climb over each shape to get from one end to the other. It is aimed at ages 5 to 12 and holds up to 15 children. The route through the shapes builds upper body strength, balance and pretend play, as children decide for themselves which way to go. The structure covers 25'5\" x 14'5\", and the safe play area is 31'5\" x 18'5\". It comes in a multi-colour scheme from our Khel-Khud collection. Galvanised pipes, roto-moulded parts, composite laminates and play rope are covered for 3 years. Share your site plan and we will mark out where it fits.",
